INT. FISH MARKET - WALK-IN FREEZER - NIGHT

Frost on everything. Hanging tuna like pale bells. Breath clouds.

MAURA KESSLER-DIAZ, 40s, black parka, lockpick case, crouches at a floor safe.

The heavy door SCRATCHES open. Light slices in.

She kills her penlight. Flattens against the shelving.

Boots. Slow.

TIBOR "TIB" NAGY, 50s, market night manager, rubber apron, a gaff hook in one fist, walks in.

He stops. Smells the air.

TIB
I know somebody's in here.

Silence. Drip. Fans.

TIB (CONT'D)
Cameras went dark an hour ago. That's not luck.

MAURA
(stepping out)
Hello, Tib.

He doesn't flinch. Raises the hook.

TIB
Maura. You left your hair dye in my sink last time.

MAURA
Brown. Not my color.

TIB
You're stealing from the wrong man.

MAURA
Everybody says that.

They circle. Tuna swing between them.

TIB
Put the picks down.

MAURA
Put the hook down.

Neither does.

TIB
Your brother used to say you talk too much.

MAURA
My brother used to say a lot of things. Then he said nothing.

Tib's jaw tightens.

TIB
That wasn't me.

MAURA
It was your safe.

He lunges. She drops the case. They collide. The shelving rattles. Fish rain.

They grapple, hook against forearm, her knee into his ribs.

TIB (CONT'D)
(grunting)
Stop it!

MAURA
You stop it!

Tib slams her into a shelf. Ice cracks loose. They both slide to the floor.

Both freeze. A distant sound: a truck engine.

TIB
That's my deliveries.

MAURA
You have deliveries at two a.m.?

TIB
Fish don't keep hours.

The engine idles. Voices outside, muffled.

They look at each other. At the safe. At the door.

MAURA
Who's out there, Tib?

TIB
(low)
Not mine.

MAURA
Then whose?

Tib lowers the hook. A fraction.

TIB
The man who owns the safe.

MAURA
You said it was yours.

TIB
I lied. Everybody does.

The door handle turns. They both dive behind the tuna rack.

They crouch shoulder to shoulder. Her breath on his collar. His hand over her mouth.

She bites it.

TIB (CONT'D)
(whisper-yelling)
Ow!

MAURA
(whisper)
Quiet!

A shadow crosses the frosted glass. Stops.

They go still. Fans hum. A fish drips onto Maura's hood.

TIB (CONT'D)
(barely audible)
When he opens the door, you take the left.

MAURA
Why would I take anything from you?

TIB
Because he kills us both if you don't.

The shadow leans in. A knuckle taps the glass. Twice.

Tib and Maura exchange a look. Then, together, they stand.

MAURA
On three.

TIB
One.

MAURA
Two.

The door swings wide.

They launch.
